---
// ABOUTME: Contribute page in the docs shell: the steps to propose a pattern and the rules a submission must meet.
// ABOUTME: Commands and rules follow CONTRIBUTING.md and AI_POLICY.md at the repository root.
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/nibzard/awesome-agentic-patterns';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Propose a pattern - Agentic Patterns"
  description="How to propose a new agent design pattern or improve an existing one."
>
  <article class="contribute-page">
    <h1>Propose a pattern</h1>
    <p class="contribute-lede">
      Each pattern is one Markdown file in <code>patterns/</code>. You add or change a file and open
      a pull request. A maintainer reviews it against the rules below.
    </p>

    <h2>Steps</h2>
    <ol class="contribute-steps">
      <li>
        <a href="/">Search the catalog</a> first. If a pattern already covers your idea, improve that
        pattern instead of adding a new one.
      </li>
      <li>
        Fork the repository and copy <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/TEMPLATE.md`}>TEMPLATE.md</a> to
        <code>patterns/&lt;your-slug&gt;.md</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Fill in the front-matter and the five sections: Problem, Solution, How to use it,
        Trade-offs, References.
      </li>
      <li>
        Validate and regenerate the site data:
        <pre><code>bun install
bun run validate:patterns:content
bun run build:data</code></pre>
      </li>
      <li>
        Commit the pattern file and the generated output together, then open a pull request. If AI
        tools helped write it, say so in the description.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Rules</h2>
    <ul class="contribute-rules">
      <li>
        The pattern must be new. It must not repeat an existing pattern with a different name.
      </li>
      <li>No promotional, sales, affiliate, or backlink content.</li>
      <li>
        Prefer neutral references: papers, standards, <code>github.com</code> repositories. Vendor links
        are accepted only when they add clear value.
      </li>
      <li>You must understand and be able to defend every line you submit.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other ways to help</h2>
    <ul class="contribute-rules">
      <li>
        Fix an error in a pattern: use <strong>Edit on GitHub</strong> on that pattern's page.
      </li>
      <li>
        Report a bug or request a feature in the <a href={`${repoUrl}/issues`}>issue tracker</a>.
      </li>
      <li>Work on the site: see <a href="/guides/help">Local development</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="contribute-refs">
      Full rules: <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING.md</a> ·
      <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/AI_POLICY.md`}>AI_POLICY.md</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .contribute-page {
    max-width: 46rem;
    line-height: var(--leading-prose);
  }

  .contribute-page h1 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
  }

  .contribute-lede {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-muted-strong);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .contribute-page h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .contribute-steps,
  .contribute-rules {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
  }

  .contribute-steps li,
  .contribute-rules li {
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
  }

  .contribute-page a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .contribute-page :not(pre) > code {
    padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--code-bg);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .contribute-page pre {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--code-block-bg);
    color: var(--code-block-fg);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .contribute-refs {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
